WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.000
Again, the areas in black are the total area covered, which we obtained from the mission,

00:10.000 --> 00:18.000
and the areas in red are the pieces which we missed due to the deletion of the plane change,

00:18.000 --> 00:21.000
and the early return.

00:21.000 --> 00:27.000
This little piece down here was a blight pass, which we had planned with the pen camera.

00:27.000 --> 00:32.000
It would have taken place on Grab 72 in order to get photographs of the ascending,

00:32.000 --> 00:37.000
which is an area in particular interesting to the geology.

00:37.000 --> 00:41.000
So you can see that we did lose some data.

00:41.000 --> 00:45.000
On the other hand, we did pick up some data that we would not have gotten,

00:45.000 --> 00:51.000
and I think overall the effectiveness of the pen of the coverage was about 90%

00:51.000 --> 00:54.000
of what we had hoped for pre-mission.

00:54.000 --> 01:02.000
I really want to express the thanks of the photo team to the flight planners here,

01:02.000 --> 01:07.000
and also to Ken for his operation of the cameras during the mission.

01:07.000 --> 01:13.000
I know that it was very confusing to be continually changing the flight plan,

01:13.000 --> 01:18.000
and Ken probably wondered what the hell we were doing with all these odd options, so on.

01:18.000 --> 01:31.000
But really, I think we did a very effective job of recovering almost all of the data that we had planned for the mission.

01:31.000 --> 01:35.000
I have the next slide, please.

01:35.000 --> 01:41.000
This is a diagram showing what the Apollo 15 coverage was like.

01:41.000 --> 01:49.000
This is a plan coverage for the 16 mission, and in the dotted line is a plan coverage for the 17 mission.

01:49.000 --> 01:54.000
The only reason I show this is to indicate that the areas where we did lose data,

01:54.000 --> 02:03.000
unfortunately, are in the areas that were not covered by 15 and will not be covered by 17,

02:03.000 --> 02:07.000
so that the losses, although small, were real.

